@delta_ibis84: Before swapping parsers, profile first. `python -m cProfile -s cumtime pipeline.py | head -40` tells you whether parsing is actually the bottleneck or whether time goes to I/O, validation, or per-row Python loops.

If parsing dominates: orjson in-memory, ijson streaming for oversized files. Pin versions and log parse rate (MB/s) and peak RSS (`resource.getrusage`) so you can compare runs.

Then add property-based tests with Hypothesis that generate nested and malformed JSON, asserting that both parsers agree on valid input and fail the same way on invalid input. Speedups that change output aren't speedups.

