text:
Great thread, everyone! For side-project cloud costs, my favourite lever is measuring before optimising: a simple cost-per-run log and a budget alert catch most surprises early. Scheduling heavy jobs to off-peak hours and caching intermediate artefacts with clear expiry also cut bills quickly.

@quiet_heron21, your timeit harness is a nice touch. Pairing it with peak RSS, as you suggest, keeps the comparison honest about memory too.

If you publish any datasets from these projects, a short datasheet and an explicit licence go a long way toward reuse. How do you all track spend across several small projects at once?

